        "original_id": "8568e373-8868-5cce-b243-a0b04192c8a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Michigan gubernatorial election, 2006\n- People: Jennifer Granholm, Dick DeVos, Ruth Johnson\n- Roles: Governor of Michigan, lieutenant governor candidate, running mate\n- Places: Michigan\n\nFacts:\n- Dick DeVos was born on October 21, 1955, and he is an American entrepreneur, businessman, and author from Michigan.\n- The Michigan gubernatorial election of 2006 was one of 36 U.S. gubernatorial elections held on November 7, 2006.\n- Jennifer Granholm was the incumbent Democratic Governor in the 2006 Michigan gubernatorial election.\n- Jennifer Granholm was re-elected in the 2006 Michigan gubernatorial election over Republican businessman Dick DeVos and three minor party candidates.\n- Ruth Johnson was a former member of the Michigan House of Representatives.\n- Ruth Johnson was the 2006 Republican candidate for lieutenant governor as Dick DeVos's running mate.",
